    - target: {fileID: 7618099258093815094, guid: e5b84f174e86f4c9bae761242c0cc40c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "[Chapter 1 General Provisions]\n\nArticle 1 (Purpose)\n\nThese terms
        and conditions are CRIEFP PTE. The purpose of LTD. (\"Company\") is to prescribe
        the rights, obligations, responsibilities, and other necessary matters between
        the Company and its members for the use of all game services provided by
        the Mobile Device and its accompanying networks, websites, and other services
        (\"Services\"). \n\nArticle 2 (Definition of Terms)\n\n1. The term \"member\"
        means a person who enters a contract for use in accordance with these terms
        and conditions and uses the services provided by the company.\n2. The term
        \"non-member\" refers to a person who uses \"service\" without joining \"member\".\n3.
        The term \"mobile device\" means a device that can be used by downloading
        or installing content through a network, and means a mobile phone, a smartphone,
        a PDA, a tablet, etc.\n4. The term \"account information\" refers to the
        member's membership number, external account information, device information,
        nickname, profile image, friend list, etc., game usage information (character
        information, item, level, goods, etc.), payment information, etc.\n5. The
        term \"content\" means any paid or free content (game and network services,
        applications, game money, game items, etc.) digitally produced by the company
        in connection with the provision of services for use as mobile devices.\n6.
        \"Paid payment\" means payment through a payment company recognized by the
        company to purchase or use content in the service.\n7. \"Open market\" means
        an e-commerce environment built to install applications and make paid payments
        on mobile devices.\n8. The term \"affiliate service\" means a service provided
        by a company through partnership with another mobile platform service provider
        and means an individual or all service provided by a mobile device using
        subscription information, profile photos, etc. of the affiliated mobile platform.\n9.
        The term \"payment company\" means a company that provides electronic payment
        methods that can be used in the open market, such as credit card and mobile
        phone payment.\n10. \"Application\" means any program that is downloaded
        or installed through a mobile device to use the services provided by the
        company.\n11. The term \"game service\" means one of the services provided
        by the company, which is a game played by a member on a mobile device and
        accompanying services.\n\nArticle 3 (Effect and amendment of terms and conditions)\n\n1.
        \"Company\" will take technical measures to ensure that \"User\" can print
        all of these terms and conditions and verify the contents of those terms
        and conditions during the \"Service\" use process.\n2. These Terms and Conditions
        are for all users who wish to use \"Service\", and \"User\" must agree to
        these Terms and Conditions before using \"Service\".\n3. \"Company\" may
        change these Terms and Conditions if necessary. If \"Company\" changes the
        terms and conditions, notify the service of notification, notice, or similar
        to the application date for a considerable period of time from 7 days before
        the application date, and notify the existing \"user\" individually by e-mail,
        text, messenger, etc. However, if individual notifications are difficult
        for the \"user\", individual notifications can be replaced by posting them
        on the notice board in the app.\n4. \"Company\" may notify \"User\" that
        it has agreed to change the terms and conditions if it does not show its
        refusal by the date of application of the change, and \"Company\" considers
        \"User\" to have agreed to the revised terms and conditions.\n5. If the \"user\"
        does not agree to the terms and conditions of the change, the \"company\"
        may terminate the contract with the \"user\" or restrict the use of the \"user\"
        service.\n\n[Chapter 2] [Registration]\n\nArticle 4 (Membership)\n\n1. The
        user applies for membership by filling out the membership information according
        to the subscription form set by the \"Service\" and expressing his/her intention
        to agree to the terms and conditions.\n2. \"Company\" may refuse to accept
        the application for subscription, and if the reason for the following is
        confirmed even after the subscription, the approval may be canceled.\n- Where
        the applicant or user is under 19 years of age.\n- Where an applicant or
        user has previously lost his/her membership status.\n- Where there is a false,
        erroneous, or omission of entry in the registration details of the applicant
        or user.\n- Where the applicant or user resides in a country where the company
        does not provide services.\n- Where an applicant or user fails to authenticate
        a password or biometric information continuously.\n- Where it is deemed that
        registering an applicant or user as a member will cause business and technical
        difficulties of the service and the company.\n- Where there are other reasons
        why it is difficult to approve the membership.\n\nArticle 5 (Withdrawal of
        membership and loss of qualification, etc.)\n\n1. \"Member\" can request
        withdrawal using the withdrawal menu within \"Service\", and \"Company\"
        will process the withdrawal of membership if the conditions announced in
        the app are met.\n\n1) If the total amount of digital assets in the \"Service\"
        is more than KRW100, you cannot withdraw.\n\n2) If there are outstanding
        transactions, including but not limited to sending and receiving within the
        \"Service\", you cannot withdraw.\n\n1. When withdrawing, \"members\" cannot
        log in to \"services\" and the use of \"services\" is restricted\n2. If you
        log in within 14 days of withdrawal, your account may be restored, but after
        that, your account will be deleted and cannot be recovered.\n3. If \"members\"
        fall under the following reasons, \"company\" may restrict and suspend membership
        qualifications.\n\n1) Where false information is registered at the time of
        application for membership;\n\n2) Where the payment for the use of the service
        of the \"company\" and other obligations borne by the members in connection
        with the use of the service of the \"company\" are not fulfilled on the due
        date;\n\n3) Where it threatens the order of use of services, such as obstructing
        the use of services by another person's \"company\" or stealing such information;\n\n4)
        Where an act is prohibited by statutes or these terms and conditions or acts
        contrary to public order and good customs using \"company\";\n\n1. After
        the \"company\" restricts or suspends its membership, the company may lose
        its membership if the same act is repeated more than twice or the reason
        is not corrected within 30 days.\n2. If the \"company\" loses its membership
        status, the membership registration is canceled. In such cases, the \"member\"
        shall be notified and given an opportunity to explain at least 30 days prior
        to the cancellation of membership registration.\n3. When withdrawal is completed,
        the member's information is removed from the service, but due to the technical
        characteristics of the blockchain, data related to the blockchain cannot
        be deleted.\n4. Since \"Service\" does not manage the user's private key,
        \"Member\" has all rights, such as membership, termination, and signature,
        and \"Member\" can cancel the \"Service\" by deleting the Private Key without
        a separate cancellation procedure.\n\nArticle 6 (Transition to Dormant Member)\n\n1.
        Unconnected \"members\" for more than a year will be converted to dormant
        accounts.\n2. Inform the customer 30 days before switching to a dormant account
        and give them the opportunity to recover their account.\n3. After three years
        of transition to a dormant account, it is separated into a \"deleted account\"
        and personal information excluding email addresses and wallet addresses is
        discarded.\n4. Inform the customer 30 days before switching to a delete account
        and give them the opportunity to recover the account.\n\n[Chapter 3. Use
        of \"Service\"]\n\nArticle 7 (\"Service\" Contents)\n\n1. Token related The
        number of tokens that users receive compensation, the calculation formula
        of tokens used to supplement their physical strength, or to purchase and
        repair items can be changed from time to time depending on the company's
        decision. In addition, the company can reverse and reverse compensation if
        it is accidentally assigned to the user, accumulated by misusing the service,
        or acquired by fraud or dishonest means.\n2. Virtual asset account management
        service\n- \"Users\" can create virtual asset accounts by signing up for
        \"services.\" At this time, the registered email address is used as the user's
        account ID, and when contact with the customer is required, it is used as
        the address to receive the email.\n- \"User\" can check the list of accounts
        held on the blockchain within \"Service\" and the balance and transaction
        details of each account. In this case, the information and market price indicated
        in legal currency corresponding to each region and setting are information
        from a third party, and the information may or may not be provided due to
        network conditions and circumstances of the third party, so the company is
        not responsible or guaranteed for the accuracy and timing of the information.\n-
        The transaction details of the account on the blockchain provided by the
        company are information that the company inquires and displays the blockchain
        network, and the accuracy and timing of the information are not responsible
        or guaranteed due to network conditions and blockchain circumstances.\n1.
        Virtual asset remittance service\n- Users can send or receive virtual assets
        based on their virtual asset address. At this time, the \"Company\" is not
        responsible for the assets deposited/transferred to the incorrectly entered
        virtual asset address. In addition, the \"company\" is not responsible for
        delays and failures in deposit/transfer due to errors in the blockchain network
        itself.\n- After the remittance is completed, it cannot be canceled, and
        the company only delivers the remittance details to the blockchain network,
        so the company is not responsible for the accuracy and completeness of the
        transaction in progress.\n1. Provision of information and publication of
        advertisements\n- \"Company\" may provide \"Members\" with a variety of information
        that \"User\" deems necessary during the use of the service by means of a
        notice or email. However, \"members\" can refuse reception at any time through
        the denial of receipt function in the email or app.\n- \"Company\" may place
        advertisements in apps, homepages, e-mails, etc. in connection with the provision
        of the service. A \"member\" who receives an e-mail with an advertisement,
        etc. may request the \"company\" to refuse the receipt.\n1. If the \"Service\"
        app installed on the \"User\" device is stopped or deleted, or the account
        information of the \"User\" stored on the device is deleted, some data of
        the \"User\" may be initialized, and in the worst case, the wallet may not
        be recovered. The \"User\" shall manage the hardware and software stability
        of the device with this in mind, and the Company shall not be responsible
        for any disadvantages caused by the \"User\" carelessness.\n2. Obligation
        of \"user\"\n- \"User\" shall comply with these Terms and all instructions
        provided by \"Company\" to \"User\" and shall comply with any applicable
        laws and regulations applicable to the use of the Service.\n- All legal rights,
        including copyrights, trademarks, patents, utility models, design rights,
        database rights and trade secrets, ownership and use/benefit rights of all
        content provided by the \"Service\" and underlying services, are owned by
        the \"Company\". Therefore, \"User\" acquires only personal, non-exclusive,
        and non-transferable limited rights to use the service within the scope of
        its use.\n- \"User\" shall never attack, disable, or disable security devices,
        etc. established by the Company or any hardware and software provider for
        the operation of the Service, using his or her knowledge or other tools.\n-
        All information collected during the service use process can be analyzed
        and utilized for the purpose of improving the \"service\" or developing new
        products and services. \"User\" allows \"Company\" to use \"Information\"
        for this purpose.\n1. Other matters\n- \"Service\" requires a user's device,
        a functioning OS, underlying software, and a reliable network, and may be
        changed, restricted, or discontinued depending on various operational, technical,
        or legal situations.\n- The use of the \"Service\" is free of charge, but
        may be converted to a fee or a separate fee depending on future operational,
        technical, or legal changes.\n- \"Company\" shall not compensate \"Users\"
        for any modification, suspension, or termination of \"Service\" unless there
        are specific reasonable reasons or applicable provisions in the relevant
        Act.\n\n[Chapter 4 Guarantee and Exemption, etc. of the Company]\n\nArticle
        8 (Scope of Company's Guarantee and Disclaimer\n\n1. \"Company\" does not
        guarantee or guarantee the following for \"Services\".\n- Risk of competition
        with other platforms\n- Risk of hacking into harmful and malicious code\n-
        Risk of negligence in keeping the buyer's own account, such as loss of key\n-
        Risk of occurrence of catastrophic events such as force majeure natural disasters\n-
        Risk due to lack of interest from companies and individuals in platforms
        and services\n- Risks arising from changes in political, social, and economic
        environments and changes in the stock or cryptocurrency market environment\n-
        Risks arising from technological advances such as advances in decryption,
        or quantum computing\n1. It is entirely up to the \"user\" to determine whether
        the \"user\" can legally trade the asset using the \"service\". The use of
        \"services\" may be restricted for natural persons, citizens, and corporations
        in areas where national laws or policies prohibit or restrict the trade of
        digital tokens.\n2. \"Company\" shall bear responsibility for damages incurred
        in connection with the use of \"Service\" in accordance with the relevant
        laws and regulations only if there is a reason attributable to \"Company\".\n3.
        In the event that the \"user\" violates these terms and conditions and causes
        damage to the \"company\", the \"user\" shall compensate for the damage to
        the \"company\".\n4. Korean law applies to the relationship between \"User\"
        and \"Company\" under these Terms and Conditions. In the event of a service-related
        dispute between the \"company\" and the \"user\", the lawsuit shall be proceeded
        with the court in accordance with the procedures prescribed by the relevant
        statutes as the competent court.\n\nSupplementary Provisions\n\nThese terms
        and conditions will come into effect on January 9, 2023."
